<report>
<line><title>Logrank and Wilcoxon tests</title></line>
<block name="outer">
<line></line>
<line><title><in>title</in><in>strata</in>:</title></line>
<block name="groups">
<line></line>
<line><u><subtotal>For group <in>grp</in></subtotal></u></line>
<line>Observed deaths = <in>obs</in></line>
<line>Extent of exposure to risk of death = <in>ext</in></line>
<line>Relative rate = <in>rel</in></line>
</block>
<line></line>
<line>test statistics:</line>
<line><in>rank</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>variance-covariance matrix:</line>
<block name="covar"><line><in>mat</in></line></block>
<line></line>
<line>Chi-square for equivalence of death rates = <in>chi</in>  <pval><in>p</in></pval></line>
<block name="trends"><line>Chi-square for trend = <in>trend</in> <pval> <in>p_trend</in></pval></line></block>
<block name="strata">
<line></line>
<line><title><in>test</in> for COMBINED STRATA</title><subtotal>:</subtotal></line>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><th>Stratum</th><th>Deaths</th><th>Extent of exposure to risk of death</th><th>Relative rate</th></tr>
<block name="stratum"><tr><td><in>grp</in></td><td><in>res</in></td><td><in>sum</in></td><td><in>tot</in></td></tr></block>
</table>
<line></line>
<line>overall chi-square = <in>chi_strata</in>  <pval><in>p_strata</in></pval></line>
<block name="strata_trend"><line>Chi-square for trend = <in>strata_trend</in><pval>  <in>p_strata_trend</in></pval></line></block>
</block>
<block name="hazards">
<line></line>
<line></line>
<line>Hazard Ratio  <ci>(approximate <in>pc</in>% confidence interval)</ci></line>
<block name="hazard"><line><in>vs</in> = <in>haz</in>  <ci>(<in>from</in> to <in>to</in>)</ci></line></block>
<block name="cml">
<line></line>
<line>Conditional maximum likelihood estimates:</line>
<line>Hazard Ratio = <in>hr</in></line>
<line><ci>Exact Fisher <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>llf</in> to <in>ulf</in></ci></line>
<line><pval>Exact Fisher one sided <in>p1f</in>, two sided <in>p2f</in></pval></line>
<line><ci>Exact mid-P <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>llm</in> to <in>ulm</in></ci></line>
<line><pval>Exact mid-P one sided <in>p1m</in>, two sided <in>p2m</in></pval></line>
</block>
</block>
</block>
</report>
